  "prompt": "To add each session's UTM values, Mailvora joins the session_start events to sessions, with an inner join: an event matches the backend session of the same visitor (visitor_id is the event's user_pseudo_id) whose session_start, in seconds since 1970, equals the event's ga_session_id, and an event with no match adds no row. Check that join for the Dublin day 4 November 2025 (by event_date), using the session_start events that carry both a user_pseudo_id and a ga_session_id. Return three columns, in this order: events_before (those session_start events), rows_after (the rows once each event is joined to its sessions row) and difference (rows_after minus events_before). Return one row. Any row order is fine.",
